## 1. Covered material and ownership

"Covered Material" means all copyrightable project code, documentation, and
other project material in the upcoming Mpv∞ release identified under
LICENSE-BOUNDARY.md that ZHINFINITY owns or has express authority from the
relevant rights holders to offer under these exact terms. It includes owned
or expressly authorized frame-interpolation code and feature updates carried
forward unchanged from earlier snapshots, as well as additions and changes.
Coverage is not limited to material newly written after a particular commit.
An authorization is effective only within its actual scope; repository control,
a copyright header, or permission to use a different licence does not establish
ownership or authority to offer these terms.

Third-party and upstream components, dependencies, bundled libraries, assets,
and contributions owned by others remain under their applicable licences and
notices. They are not included merely because they appear in this release or
are combined with Covered Material. Any separate offer under these terms for
another rights holder's project contribution requires documented express
authority for that particular material and these terms; it does not remove
that holder's original notices or independently applicable grants. Unresolved
ownership or authority is not a basis for claiming coverage. In mixed files,
these terms apply only to the portions ZHINFINITY owns or is expressly
authorized to license this way, not automatically to the whole file.

This is the proposed licence offer for Covered Material in the upcoming
release, not a claim that previously licensed code becomes exclusively
permission-only. Earlier grants, including grants for unchanged code carried
into this release, remain available as explained in section 4.
See THIRD_PARTY_SOURCE.md and LICENSE-BOUNDARY.md for the inventory and gaps.

## 2. App use is permitted; code reuse and republication require permission

### 2.1 Permission for everyone to use official app releases

ZHINFINITY grants everyone a nonexclusive, worldwide, royalty-free permission
to download, install, update, and run official, unmodified Mpv∞ app releases
distributed by ZHINFINITY or an expressly authorized distributor, on devices
they own or are authorized to use. This includes the copies reasonably
necessary to install, operate, update, and back up the app for their own use.
Ordinary app use is permitted for personal, educational, organizational, and
commercial purposes. No individual permission request is required for these
activities. These terms do not restrict media or data merely used with the app.

This end-user permission is for using the app, not for reusing its source code,
making derivative apps, sharing copies with others, rehosting APKs, or publishing
the app or a modified version in an app store or elsewhere. Sharing a link to
an official download is allowed; redistributing the app itself is not granted
by this section. Sections 4 and 5 preserve independently applicable rights.

### 2.2 Prior written permission for code reuse and republication

Except for section 2.1 and the rights preserved in sections 4 and 5, no licence
is granted to copy, reproduce, modify, adapt, create derivative works from,
reuse, redistribute, sublicense, sell, monetize, publish, upload, or otherwise
make available any Covered Material, in whole or in part, in source or binary
form. Each such activity requires prior written permission from ZHINFINITY.

This requirement applies to commercial and noncommercial activities alike,
including copying source code for private projects, reposting, app-store
publication, advertising-supported distribution, and incorporation into another
project. Public access, attribution, absence of a fee, or a failure to respond
to a request is not permission. The app-use grant in section 2.1 does not grant
general source-code reuse or republication rights.

Any permission must expressly identify the material and authorized activities
and their scope; section 2.1 itself provides that permission for ordinary app
use. Section 5 acknowledges GitHub platform rights without a separate request.
No permission grants rights outside its scope or rights owned by others.
No separate patent, trademark, branding, or endorsement rights are granted by
these terms beyond any rights necessarily implied by the express app-use grant.

## 3. Attribution and no false authorship

Any use authorized under these terms must preserve applicable copyright,
author, licence, and third-party notices, and identify modifications and their
authors without presenting the original work as their own. You must not falsely
claim to be the original creator or author of material created by others, or
suggest that ZHINFINITY endorses your version without written authorization.
Attribution does not replace the permission required by section 2. These
conditions do not purport to impose new restrictions on previously licensed
material or independently licensed third-party material.
Ordinary app users do not need to publish a separate attribution statement;
leaving the app's built-in notices intact satisfies this section for their use.

## 4. Earlier grants and third-party rights are preserved

These terms do not withdraw, narrow, replace, or amend licences or permissions
already granted for earlier snapshots or for material contained in them.
Recipients may continue to exercise those rights subject to their original
conditions, including rights in material carried forward unchanged into a new
snapshot. Previously published AGPL-3.0-or-later and PolyForm Noncommercial
versions retain their respective terms. The exact root licence of baseline
commit 7015805f6831cbf8a9fc2e6d5dd5c70af209b638 is retained in
HISTORICAL-LICENSE-POLYFORM-BASELINE.md; the prior AGPL text is retained in
HISTORICAL-LICENSE-AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt. Historical copies are references, not
new blanket grants for later Covered Material.

Earlier grants are not limited to people who already made a fork or local copy.
Anyone entitled to rely on an earlier licence may continue to do so, including
where that licence permits obtaining copies from other recipients. A person
exercising such rights must satisfy that licence, but need not obtain separate
permission under these terms for acts it already permits. Conversely, an older
licence does not automatically license later additions it never covered.

All independently applicable third-party licences remain effective, including
MIT, BSD, Apache, LGPL, MPL, PSF, and OFL terms. In particular, nothing here
restricts modification, replacement, relinking, or reverse engineering for
debugging modifications to LGPL-covered components where required by their
licences, or any associated access to required source or relinkable material.
These terms cannot substitute for compliance with those obligations.

## 5. Law and hosting-platform rights

Nothing here restricts rights that applicable law makes available independently
of permission, including applicable copyright exceptions. Nothing here limits
rights already granted under the terms of the hosting platform, including
GitHub's rights to host the repository and its users' rights to view and fork a
public repository through GitHub's functionality. GitHub's built-in public-
repository viewing and forking, including a fork under a user's own GitHub
account, are expressly acceptable to ZHINFINITY; no separate permission request
is needed for those platform-authorized activities. This acknowledges platform
rights, not a separate general source-reuse or publication licence. A public
fork may itself be visible on GitHub; its existence is not permission to
repackage or publish the code or app elsewhere. Those platform rights do not
by themselves authorize external publication, APK rehosting, app-store release,
or reuse outside their scope. Sections 2.1 and 4 and other independent rights
continue to apply. These terms cannot technically prevent copying or infringement.

## 6. Permission requests

No request is needed for the ordinary app use expressly allowed by section 2.1.
No request is needed for GitHub viewing/forking within section 5 or for an
activity authorized by the preserved rights in sections 4 and 5.
For activities requiring separate permission under section 2.2, follow this
request process:

Contact the repository owner, ZHINFINITY, through the contact channels listed
at https://github.com/ZHINFINITY. Identify the exact source revision or files,
your intended activities, how and where you will distribute them, and whether
you intend commercial use or monetization. Do not include private information
in a public issue. Wait for an express written grant before proceeding.

